  "limitations": [
    "History remains a best-effort 200-row view, not an atomic snapshot/live join or durable replay.",
    "Relative aging is a one-second active-browser display tick, not server retention or reliable frozen-browser wall time; it does not dispatch queries or acknowledgements.",
    "Export remains a separate full-history query and is not an exact copy of displayed rows.",
    "Export MIME/filename checks do not validate arbitrary payload contents, sanitize spreadsheet formulas or add a byte budget.",
    "Export/deletion waiting is 20 seconds and unread/read acknowledgement waiting is ten seconds, including body consumption; cancellation cannot undo a dispatched server mutation or bound its transaction duration.",
    "Read acknowledgement still marks ALL events of the current account, including filtered-out and undisplayed records. No per-record IDs, cutoff or durable confirmation guarantee added.",
    "Acknowledgement failure stops automatic retries in the same scope; explicit retry or a new filter/navigation context can try again.",
    "Deletion retains typed confirmation, captured exact category/severity/time scope, existing owner/CSRF boundary, and no automatic retry or broadened failed query.",
    "A confirmed deletion response is the existing Engine acknowledgement, not new proof of cross-process SQL durability.",
    "Existing backend event tests are memory/loopback boundary regressions; full Rust, SDK runtime, database, deployment and kernel acceptance remain outside this pass.",
    "Earlier release and acceptance results remain historical and are not included in current-source or release-artifact acceptance."
  ],
